MiOS room input for Hypr3D (applies after hypr3d-mios-pip-theatre.patch; spec docs/design/mios-global-bindings-final.md P1).

1. The [keybindings.global.controller.room] verbs (C-14a), as dispatchers (hypr3d:cancel, hypr3d:sprint,
   hypr3d:recenter) and Lua functions next to input_owner/input_capture:
   - hl.plugin.hypr3d.cancel() backs out one level, innermost first: an active grab or resize, then the CRT window
     picker (now a tracked child in its own process group, titles passed as argv, never shell source), then the room
     cursor. It returns what it cancelled ("resize", "grab", "picker", "cursor" or "none").
   - hl.plugin.hypr3d.sprint([toggle|on|off]) latches the keyboard sprint speed until it is turned off or the room
     closes. It returns the new state.
   - hl.plugin.hypr3d.recenter() eases the camera onto the focused room window (else the window aim focus last
     selected, since looking away clears focus; else the nearest room window; else it levels the view) with
     [config.player].recenter_seconds.
   All three change nothing while the room does not own input or a captured window does (the ownership contract).
2. Face the viewer ([config.windows] face_viewer, face_distance, theatre_face_distance, face_seconds,
   face_hysteresis): a PiP whose centre is within its viewing distance of the camera (2 m, Theatre 4 m) turns its
   plane normal toward the camera POSITION and follows it as the camera moves; outside it eases back to the pose it
   was placed with. Every change is an exponential ease, a hysteresis band stops boundary flapping, and grabs,
   resizes, the view morph and the fullscreen passthrough own the pose while they run. Saved room poses and the
   Theatre's restore pose record the placed pose, never a facing turn. The pure math is src/World/FaceViewer.hpp,
   checked by tests/mios-face-viewer.cpp in ctest.
3. export_layout() gains room_input (sprint, gesture, resize, drag, cursor, picker, recentering and the face
   settings) and per-window pip, facing, base_yaw and base_pitch, for the live checks.

